9,Tibetan Music | Himalayan Temple | Instrumental Asian MusicMugom dialect - WikiwandTibetan Music & Audio — Stream & Download Traditional Music ...Mugom–Karmarong language - WikipediaMusic - Modern Tibetan Studies Research Guide - Research ...,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J9dAmDy3jWE,"Dec 22, 2017 · If you're interested in hearing more relaxing music please check out the first song I've written for my new relaxing music channel, Relax & Vibe, here: https... Mugom language, also known as Mugom-ket, is the Sino-Tibetan language of the Mugali people of Mugu district in Nepal. Stream rare recordings of traditional Tibetan instruments, monastic chanting, and contemporary Tibetan artists. Mugom–Karmarong is the Sino-Tibetan language variety of the Tibetan people of Mugu district in Nepal. This language variety represents two dialects Mugom and Karmarong, which are spoken by distinct ethnicities and are separate languages in the perceptions of these groups. The resource provides a wealth of materials for the interdisciplinary study of ethnomusicology; whether the focus is on music, anthropology, dance, religion or spirituality.",Mugali,Sino-Tibetan
